<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chrŏnĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρονικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to time</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libri,</span>”
				<i>chronicles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 21, 1</span></i>
			; so also <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chrŏnĭca</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ χρονικά</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35, 9,
				35, § 58</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 17,
				4, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 15,
				1</span></i>; and in sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in primo chronico,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 21, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morbi,</span>”
				<i>chronic</i>, <i>lingering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 4, 7</span></i>
			; opp. acuti morbi.— Hence the work of Caelius
			Aurelianus is entitled De morbis acutis et chronicis.</div>
